18:08:06Z","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/21007#issuecomment-2940931493","id":2940931493,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/21007","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDODGgK6M6vSw2l","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/2940931493/reactions"},"updated_at":"2025-06-04T18:08:06Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/2940931493","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62390731?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pxanthopoulos/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pxanthopoulos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pxanthopoulos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pxanthopoulos/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pxanthopoulos","id":62390731,"login":"pxanthopoulos","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyMzkwNzMx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pxanthopoulos/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pxanthopoulos/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pxanthopoulos/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pxanthopoulos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pxanthopoulos/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pxanthopoulos","user_view_type":"public"}}],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author_association":"NONE","body":"### What happened?\n\nHi. I'm trying to compile and run a Phi model to analyze memory allocation (constants, transients, etc.).\n\nWhile using `iree-run-module`, I encountered what seems to be a bug in how it traces some commands with the flag `--trace_execution=true`.\n\nThe final IR of the compilation can be found [here](https://gist.github.com/pxanthopoulos/5fe8228bce82193c6fac051d2044ba9f). In line 2399 of the IR, there is the call for the device allocation for the constants (5259886592 B = ~4.9 GiB). This is the allocation operation that is actually executed in the conditional statement where the module tries 2 ways to allocate that memory (this can be seen in the execution trace later).\n\nIn line 69 of the execution [output](https://gist.github.com/pxanthopoulos/11f932d023764a6b7f190607a542e154), we can see the corresponding call for the device allocation mentioned before. However, the allocation size has changed from 5259886592 to 964919296.\n\nI confirmed in 2 ways that the correct number is 5259886592 (by looking at the composite attribute at the top of the IR) and that it is actually the allocation size (by looking at a cuda nsight report).\n\nI believe the tracer incorrectly assumes the argument (allocation size) is stored in a single 32-bit register.\n\nIn line 69 of the execution output, where the allocation request is, we can see that register %i4 contains the allocation size. However, in line 7, this register is shown as part of a group of 2 registers, %i4 and %i5 for a total of 64 bits. These registers combined contain the correct value.\n5259886592 is represented by 33 bits and if truncated to 32 bits and 1 register, becomes 964919296, which is why I think the tracer incorrectly parses the arguments.\n\n5259886592 (0x139838000) → lower 32 bits = 0x39838000 = 964919296\n\n### Steps to reproduce your issue\n\nI downloaded the model and converted it to onnx via this [script](https://gist.github.com/pxanthopoulos/b3c02cec0e9c5ff9d7bfab3f67fbc96e).\n\nThen I imported it to MLIR via `iree-import-onnx`.\n\nThen I compiled it using the following command:\n\n```\niree-compile --iree-pretty-debuginfo \\\n            --iree-disable-threading \\\n            --iree-print-ir-after=iree-vm-ordinal-allocation \\\n            --iree-print-ir-module-scope \\\n            --iree-hal-target-device=cuda \\\n            --iree-cuda-target=cuda[0] \\\n            --iree-cuda-target=sm_70 \\\n            model.mlir -o model.vmfb 2>&1 > final-ir.mlir\n```\nAnd ran it using the following command:\n\n```\niree-run-module --trace_execution=true \\\n                --print_statistics=true \\\n                --device=cuda \\\n                --module=model.vmfb \\\n                --function=main_graph \\\n                --input=\\\"2x512xi64=3\\\" \\\n                --input=\\\"2x512xi64=1\\\" > execution-output.txt 2>&1\n```\n\n### What component(s) does this issue relate to?\n\nRuntime\n\n### Version information\n\nI am in commit hash `33f5b3178dda4322464e0d1e3ff1ac12833c9d7a`.\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_","closed_at":null,"closed_by":null,"comments":2,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/21007/comments","created_at":"2025-06-04T17:46:31Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/21007/events","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/21007","id":3118610668,"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"total_blocking":0},"issue_field_values":[],"labels":[{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"d73a4a","default":false,"description":"Something isn't working","id":1553038945,"name":"bug 🐞","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNTUzMDM4OTQ1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/labels/bug%20%F0%9F%90%9E"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/21007/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":null,"node_id":"I_kwDODGgK6M654jjs","number":21007,"performed_via_github_app":null,"pinned_comment":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/21007/reactions"},"repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree","state":"open","state_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"completed":0